  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Fresh-Start Band",
    "overview": "The site is the logo, laid out flat as full-bleed bands. Off-white paper and two blues taken from the logo's arc alternate down the page so every section change is obvious on a phone, and the logo's leaf green is the one accent: it fills the things you press and nothing else. There are no photos (the business has no real work photos), so the depth comes from the colour of the bands, a faint diagonal line texture on the hero and footer, and two white objects that sit on the blue: the quote form card and the logo on its white circle.\n\nThe density is phone-first and generous: one column, 64px between bands on phones and 96px on desktop, big tap targets (44px minimum, 56px for main buttons), and only one control of each kind in view at a time. Headings are Cal Sans at a single weight; everything you read is the system stack at 16/1.7. Motion is spent in two places: the hero H1 bounces in letter by letter, and content below the first screen rises 12px into place once. Nothing else moves.\n\nThe system follows the owner's house calm band style (`~/.claude/skills/pitch-site/references/calm-photo-style.md`), with the logo's green standing in for that style's usual warm gold accent.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Full-bleed bands in a fixed order: paper header, navy textured hero, paper, navy, paper, navy, deep textured footer.",
      "One accent (leaf green) used as a fill; a darker green only when green has to be text on paper.",
      "Cal Sans display at weight 400 only, system body at 16/1.7.",
      "Soft, borderless shapes: 24px cards, 10px fields, full pills, circles.",
      "Links that are whole rows; the only thing that changes on hover is a 44px arrow circle.",
      "One contact channel at a time, switched from a single CONFIG block."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Fill-Only Green Rule",
        "body": "Leaf green (`green`) is a fill. On paper it never appears as text; use `green-ink`. On navy it may be text only at heading size.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Band Contrast Rule",
        "body": "Bands alternate light and dark so a new section is obvious; two navy bands are never adjacent, and every navy band is followed by paper or the deep footer.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Weight Rule",
        "body": "Cal Sans is used at 400 only. Hierarchy comes from size and colour, never from bolding the display face.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tappable Voice Rule",
